if a party has more than one place of business,
the place of business is that which has the closest relationship to the
contract and its performance, having regard to the circumstances known to or
contemplated by the parties at any time before or at the conclusion of the
contract;

if the contract of sale involves carriage of the
goods—in handing the goods over to the first carrier for transmission to
the buyer;

at the time of the conclusion of the contract the
buyer knew or could not have been unaware of the right or claim;
or

in respect of late delivery, within a reasonable
time after he has become aware that delivery has been
made;

in doing all the acts which could reasonably be
expected of him in order to enable the seller to make delivery;
and

in respect of late performance by the buyer,
before the seller has become aware that performance has been rendered;
or

if the goods or part of the goods have perished
or deteriorated as a result of the examination provided for in article 38;
or
